[DAY-BY-DAY SCHEDULE]

--- DAY 1: SAKYO-KU ---
  Insider Tip: Local tip: Visit Sakyo-ku's small artisan espresso bars before 10 AM for fresh pastries straight from the stone oven.
  • [Morning (09:30 AM)] Kyoto Traditional Crafts Center (Kyoto Museum of Crafts and Design) (FREE)
      Discover a wide array of traditional Kyoto crafts, from textiles and ceramics to lacquerware and dolls.
  • [Afternoon (02:00 PM)] Ginkaku-ji (Silver Pavilion) & Philosopher's Path ($5.00)
      Explore the elegant Zen temple with its unique sand garden, followed by a scenic walk along the cherry blossom-lined Philosopher's Path.

--- DAY 2: FUSHIMI-KU ---
  Insider Tip: Insider advice: The pedestrian alleys in Fushimi-ku are best explored on foot right around golden hour for photography.
  • [Morning (09:30 AM)] Fushimi Inari-taisha (FREE)
      Explore the iconic thousands of vermilion torii gates winding up Mount Inari.
  • [Late Afternoon (04:30 PM)] ✨ Hidden Gem: Secret Garden & Vintage Book Arcade (FREE)
      A tucked-away historic glass arcade with antique bookstalls and a quiet courtyard fountain.

--- DAY 3: HIGASHIYAMA ---
  Insider Tip: Secret spot: Look out for historic courtyard passages tucked behind the main boulevard for quiet artisan cafes.
